times draw distance. 80 lbs sounds impressive--but on a pistol sized
crossbow it probably results in not much energy. Mac's hand crossbow is
cocked by turning a sort of big wing nut, attached to a threaded rod to
which the nut (the thing that holds the string drawn) is attached. That
gives you a lot of mechanical advantage--and you need it for a bow stiff
