This led me to some interesting whacky speculation about getting
around legal bans on automatic weapons and armour-piercing bullets 
in the US.

Take a hand crossbow and a replica automatic pistol. hack off
pistol barrel and replace everything forward of breech with a thickly
wound coil. Take magazine, fill with blanks, and add some magnetized
iron filings to the blanks. For safety's sake put some kind of target
chamber on the end of the coil to absorb the shrapnel. 

Take hand crossbow. Replace wing but with high-torque electric motor.
Ensure that crossbow is magazine-fed. Place solenoid or reed switch
behind trigger so that when trigger is pulled, switch closes.

Switch runs to handgun-turned-MHD generator. Pulls trigger, fires
blank, produces _big_ current pulse in coil, feeds to capacitor then
drains into electric motor in crossbow. Result? A fully-automatic
crossbow. Armour-piercing, too. 

'Course if this gadget is illegal (it fires blanks, after all), you
could always power it off a car battery in a rucksack ...


