for such a thread.
Everyone's trying to figure out how we can learn
special "mental" responses that we can use to
control machines -- any kind of "hands-off" operation
will do.  The implications for quadriplegic individuals
are obvious....  So far, detection and control activities
are pretty basic -- cursor movement studies, stuff like
that -- but its DOABLE!  The biggest problem appears
to be detection -- EEG's are such a mess, and there are
SOOOO many neurons and connections...
